Given that, 1 is a root of $a x^2+b x+c=0\begin{aligned}
&amp; \Rightarrow \quad a+b+c=0 \\
&amp; \therefore \quad E_1: a+b+c=0 \text { is true. }
\end{aligned}$
Since $\cos \theta, \sin \theta$ are the roots of
$\begin{aligned}
&amp; a x^2+b x+c=0 \\
\therefore \quad &amp; \sin \theta+\cos \theta=-\frac{b}{a} \\
\text { and } \sin \theta \cos \theta= &amp; \frac{c}{a}
\end{aligned}$
On squaring both sides of equation (i)
$\begin{array}{rlrl} &amp; (\sin \theta+\cos \theta)^2 &amp; =\frac{b^2}{a^2} \\
\Rightarrow \sin ^2 \theta+\cos ^2 \theta+2 \sin \theta \cos \theta &amp; =\frac{b^2}{a^2} \\
\Rightarrow &amp; 1+2\left(\frac{c}{a}\right) &amp; =\frac{b^2}{a^2} \\
\Rightarrow &amp; 2 \cdot \frac{c}{a} &amp; =\frac{b^2-a^2}{a^2} \\
\Rightarrow &amp; -a^2+b^2 &amp; =2 a c \\
\therefore &amp; E_2: b^2-a^2 &amp; =2 a c \text { is true }
\end{array}
$\Rightarrow E_1$ and $E_2$ both are true.$

